Update 2026-09-07 (Workspace-Refactor, upstream bb35131 branch workspace-refactor): explicit memory
model. weirdike_ctx = small long-lived state (IKE-SA state objects in 2 slots, Child-SA slots); every
message-sized buffer lives in a separate WORKSPACE block (SA_INIT transcript, per-IKE-SA request/
response caches, RX plaintext, TX build area, crypto scratch). API break: weirdike_init(ctx_mem,
ctx_len, ws_mem, ws_len, ...) fully caller-owned; weirdike_new(..., const weirdike_mem_t *mem) with a
provider alloc(bytes, alignment, kind)/free(ptr, kind); weirdike_mem_req() reports sizes+alignment;
ike_platform_t lost alloc/free. Parsers return views (ike_span_t) into the workspace. ESP:
esp_session_init(..., scratch, cap) takes a host-placed RX scratch (>= ESP_MAX_PACKET); esp_open()
takes a scratch too. WeirdOS (ipsec_runtime.cpp): CONTEXT -> internal RAM, WORKSPACE -> PSRAM,
ESP scratch -> PSRAM (one per session slot). Reason: 'Stack protection fault' in loopTask on the
P4 while handling the IKE_AUTH response (largest frame 9680 B before, 976 B after, P4 toolchain -Os).

